      "message": "I am fine. It aligns with what we have today. \n\nIt will map to \n```\n[\"Status\"][\"State\"] \u003d\n            resource::State::Degraded;\n```\nThis, Present, Available, Enabled all map to the same Redfish \"Status\"\"State\" property so it isn\u0027t ideal for a bmcweb side but workable. \nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/bmcweb/+/94396 is the bmcweb code adding Degraded.\n\nThe ideal solution from a bmcweb side is an enum property called like State which can be values  Enabled, Absent, Unavailable, Disabled, Degraded. \n\nThe complete list from Redfish:\n```\n      \"State\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n                \"Enabled\",\n                \"Disabled\",\n                \"StandbyOffline\",\n                \"StandbySpare\",\n                \"InTest\",\n                \"Starting\",\n                \"Absent\",\n                \"UnavailableOffline\",\n                \"Deferring\",\n                \"Quiesced\",\n                \"Updating\",\n                \"Qualified\",\n                \"Degraded\"\n            ],\n```\nFrom http://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Resource.json#/definitions/Status\n\n\nOther interfaces mapping to this same Redfish Status State:\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/4d2db8cc64f98154cf7e83eab13f6c86014d6992/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Item.interface.yaml#L14\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Decorator/Availability.interface.yaml\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Object/Enable.interface.yaml",
